[
  {
    "sha": "d0e959385e0d28d1381733eb25551d8f0b413259",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOMVotWtoAKGQwZTk1OTM4NWUwZDI4ZDEzODE3MzNlYjI1NTUxZDhmMGI0MTMyNTk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Paul A. Clarke",
        "email": "pclarke@ventanamicro.com",
        "date": "2025-10-31T16:25:05Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Paul A. Clarke",
        "email": "paul.clarke@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2026-02-10T15:10:55Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(data): extension Svadu does not conflict with Svade\n\nSvadu, roughly, preempts Svade:\n> If the Svadu extension is implemented, the ADUE bit controls whether hardware updating of PTE A/D bits\n> is enabled for S-mode and G-stage address translations. When ADUE=1, hardware updating of PTE A/D\n> bits is enabled during S-mode address translation, and the implementation behaves as though the Svade\n> extension were not implemented for S-mode address translation. When the hypervisor extension is\n> implemented, if ADUE=1, hardware updating of PTE A/D bits is enabled during G-stage address\n> translation, and the implementation behaves as though the Svade extension were not implemented for G-\n> stage address translation. When ADUE=0, the implementation behaves as though Svade were implemented\n> for S-mode and G-stage address translation.\n\nSigned-off-by: Paul A. Clarke <pclarke@ventanamicro.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "b987a0c863de0a4447aaa8c83d5525706d574314",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-unified-db/git/trees/b987a0c863de0a4447aaa8c83d5525706d574314"
